<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Changes">Changes</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/Konar_quo_Maten?section=6&amp;veaction=edit" title="Edit section: Changes" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/w/Konar_quo_Maten?action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Changes"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<table class="wikitable mw-collapsible sortable" style="max-width:800px">
<tbody><tr>
<th>Date
</th>
<th class="unsortable">Changes
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="26 March 2025"><a href="/w/26_March" title="26 March">26&#160;March</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2025" title="2025">2025</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:Poll_83_QoL_Changes" title="Update:Poll 83 QoL Changes">Update</a>&#160;|&#160;<a href="/w/Poll:Poll_83_-_Castle_Wars,_New_Player_Changes_%26_More" title="Poll:Poll 83 - Castle Wars, New Player Changes &amp; More">poll</a>)
</td>
<td>
<p>The <a href="/w/Slayer_cape" title="Slayer cape">Slayer cape</a>'s perk now guarantees the same location from tasks assigned by Konar quo Maten.
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="28 February 2019"><a href="/w/28_February" title="28 February">28&#160;February</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:QoL_and_CoX_Changes" title="Update:QoL and CoX Changes">Update</a>)
</td>
<td>
<ul><li>Konar will no longer assign Black, Red, Blue or Green dragons within the Kourend Catacombs if the player has under 100 combat</li>
<li>Konar will no longer assign Fire giants in the Waterfall Dungeon to players who haven't yet completed the Waterfall Quest</li></ul>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="7 February 2019"><a href="/w/7_February" title="7 February">7&#160;February</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:X_Marks_The_Spot" title="Update:X Marks The Spot">Update</a>&#160;|&#160;<a href="/w/Poll:Old_School_Content_Poll_63:_Kebos_-_Post_Launch_Changes" title="Poll:Old School Content Poll 63: Kebos - Post Launch Changes">poll</a>)
</td>
<td>
<p>Loot from Konar's drop table are replaced by <a href="/w/Brimstone_key" title="Brimstone key">brimstone keys</a>; the loot has now been moved to the <a href="/w/Brimstone_chest" title="Brimstone chest">brimstone chest</a> which the key accesses.
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="21 January 2019"><a href="/w/21_January" title="21 January">21&#160;January</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:Revised_Post_Kebos_Poll_Blog" title="Update:Revised Post Kebos Poll Blog">Update</a>)
</td>
<td><span style="color:white;background:#ee4231;font-size:80%;font-weight:bold;text-transform:uppercase;border-radius:3px;padding:2px 5px;">Hotfix</span>
<p>Konar's drop table was re-tweaked, removing <a href="/w/Adamant_bolts(unf)" title="Adamant bolts(unf)">adamant</a> and <a href="/w/Runite_bolts_(unf)" title="Runite bolts (unf)">runite bolts</a> and reintroducing <a href="/w/Dragon_dart_tips" class="mw-redirect" title="Dragon dart tips">dragon dart tips</a> and <a href="/w/Magic_logs" title="Magic logs">magic logs</a>, a bug resulting in noted drops being received in unnoted form was fixed.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-6" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-6"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>4<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup>
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="17 January 2019"><a href="/w/17_January" title="17 January">17&#160;January</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:Kebos_Graphical_Changes_and_Other_Fixes" title="Update:Kebos Graphical Changes and Other Fixes">Update</a>)
</td>
<td>
<p>Slayer reward unlocks that apply to Konar quo Maten now correctly say so on the Slayer Unlock menu.
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="14 January 2019"><a href="/w/14_January" title="14 January">14&#160;January</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:Konar_Loot_Table_Balancing" title="Update:Konar Loot Table Balancing">Update</a>)
</td>
<td><span style="color:white;background:#ee4231;font-size:80%;font-weight:bold;text-transform:uppercase;border-radius:3px;padding:2px 5px;">Hotfix</span>
<p>Konar's drop table was tweaked once again. Rune drops, <a href="/w/Yew_logs" title="Yew logs">yew logs</a>, and <a href="/w/Crystal_keys" class="mw-redirect" title="Crystal keys">crystal keys</a> were entirely removed from the drop table. The weighting of pure essence was reduced from 5 to 1, making it a far less likely drop. Additionally, the <a href="/w/Alchemical_Hydra" title="Alchemical Hydra">Alchemical Hydra</a> gained access to Konar's drop table. The Lizardman Shaman Caves for Konar Slayer tasks have been replaced with a Molch area. The caves are now covered by the Lizardmen Settlement area.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-7" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-7"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>5<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup>
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="11 January 2019"><a href="/w/11_January" title="11 January">11&#160;January</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />(<a href="/w/Update:Konar_Loot_Table_Balancing" title="Update:Konar Loot Table Balancing">Update</a>)
</td>
<td>
<p>The average value of rolling Konar's drop table was reduced by 30%, removing several drops, whilst introducing pieces of the <a href="/w/Mystic_robes#Dusk" title="Mystic robes">Mystic robes (dusk)</a> set to the drop table.
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-sort-value="10 January 2019"><a href="/w/10_January" title="10 January">10&#160;January</a>&#160;<a href="/w/2019" title="2019">2019</a><br />
</td>
<td><span style="color:white;background:#ee4231;font-size:80%;font-weight:bold;text-transform:uppercase;border-radius:3px;padding:2px 5px;">Hotfix</span>
<p>An extremely rare drop of 2,500 <a href="/w/Saradomin_brew" title="Saradomin brew">Saradomin brews</a> was removed from Konar's drop table shortly after release.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-8" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-8"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>6<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup>
</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Trivia">Trivia</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/Konar_quo_Maten?section=7&amp;veaction=edit" title="Edit section: Trivia" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/w/Konar_quo_Maten?action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Trivia"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul><li>Konar is the only confirmed female <a href="/w/Kahlith" title="Kahlith">Kahlith</a> encountered in-game.</li>
<li>Konar is one of the only left-handed characters in the game.</li>
<li>Konar is implied to be a major character in the short story <a href="/w/Transcript:A_Curious_Client" title="Transcript:A Curious Client">A Curious Client</a> from the <a href="/w/Kourend_Chronicles" title="Kourend Chronicles">Kourend Chronicles</a>, in which she's involved in the hiding of the <a href="/w/Ancient_casket" title="Ancient casket">Ancient casket</a> that <a href="/w/Veos" title="Veos">Veos</a> has player find in <a href="/w/X_Marks_the_Spot" title="X Marks the Spot">X Marks the Spot</a>.</li></ul>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="References">References</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/Konar_quo_Maten?section=8&amp;veaction=edit" title="Edit section: References" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/w/Konar_quo_Maten?action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: References"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="reflist hideQuotes"><div class="mw-references-wrap"><ol class="references">
<li id="cite&#95;note-1"><span class="mw-cite-backlink"><b><a href="#cite_ref-1">^</a></b></span> <span class="reference-text"><span class="citation twitter">Jagex. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/101215">Mod Ash's Twitter account</a>. 3 February 2023.  Archived from <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1621613665072910337">the original</a> on 4 February 2023. Mod Ash: "Yes, it's an equal chance for each of the areas you're eligible to access." </span></span>
</li>
<li id="cite&#95;note-2"><span class="mw-cite-backlink"><b><a href="#cite_ref-2">^</a></b></span> <span class="reference-text"><span class="citation twitter">Jagex. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/108660">Mod Ash's Twitter account</a>. 29 April 2019.  Archived from <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1122846921331224576">the original</a> on 4 March 2023. Mod Ash: "(...) Abyssal demons will accept Fairy Tale II for abyss access." </span></span>
</li>
<li id="cite&#95;note-4"><span class="mw-cite-backlink"><b><a href="#cite_ref-4">^</a></b></span> <span class="reference-text"><span class="citation twitter">Jagex. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102411">Mod Ash's Twitter account</a>. 27 August 2020.  Archived from <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1298524179629838337">the original</a> on 27 August 2020. Mod Ash: "They do indeed require both of those. There isn't a limit on how many distinct requirements a task may have." </span></span>
</li>
<li id="cite&#95;note-6"><span class="mw-cite-backlink"><b><a href="#cite_ref-6">^</a></b></span> <span class="reference-text"><span class="citation twitter">Jagex. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102716">Old School RuneScape's Twitter account</a>. 21 January 2019.  Archived from <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/1087388290397794304">the original</a> on 29 May 2020. Old School RuneScape: ""A bug resulting certain drops not appearing noted as intended has been hotfixed."" </span></span>
</li>
<li id="cite&#95;note-7"><span class="mw-cite-backlink"><b><a href="#cite_ref-7">^</a></b></span> <span class="reference-text"><span class="citation twitter">Jagex. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/103571">Old School RuneScape's Twitter account</a>. 14 January 2019.  Archived from <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/1084834960543043585">the original</a> on 25 May 2020. </span></span>
</li>
<li id="cite&#95;note-8"><span class="mw-cite-backlink"><b><a href="#cite_ref-8">^</a></b></span> <span class="reference-text"><span class="citation twitter">Jagex. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/103128">Mod Ash's Twitter account</a>. 11 January 2019.  Archived from <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1083515413793783809">the original</a> on 29 May 2020. Mod Ash: "It was there on launch, but it was removed shortly after. It was also extremely rare." </span></span>
</li>
</ol></div></div>
